      "raw_response": "Claim: Osteocytes have an essential role in G-CSF induced HSPC mobilization.\n\nANSWER: SUPPORTED. The study by Sosiak et al. demonstrates that the bone marrow niche, particularly osteocytes, plays a critical role in the egress of HSPCs in response to G-CSF, and their absence leads to failure in mobilization.\n\nSource: Sosiak, J., et al. (2013). Granulocyte colony-stimulating factor induces changes in osteocytes that precede osteoblast changes and controls hematopoietic stem/progenitor cell egress from bone marrow. Science, 342(6159), 124312.\n\nConfidence Level: High\n\nDue to the direct evidence presented in the study, which includes surgical sympathectomy and targeted ablation experiments showing the necessity of osteocytes for G-CSF induced HSPC mobilization, the claim is strongly supported by the research findings.",
